#{[17592186527927 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}, & x=5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}, & x=10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=8.$"] [17592186527950 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.45, & y=4 \\\\ 0.55, & y=6 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=8]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,8)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|8}=5.1.$"] [17592186527976 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0.4, & x=1 \\\\ 0.6, & x=2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=1.6.$"] [17592186529138 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2+y-x}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5-2x}{6}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=1].$"] [17592186529166 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3(x+y)}{4}, & 0<x\\le 2y,\\,\\,0<y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\ri