eter $s,$ the solution of the new system is\n\n${X}_{1}(s)=\\frac{2(2s-3)}{s(s-5)},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=${{field-1}}."] [17592186544811 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following conditional probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{2x+3} & \\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x+1\\le y\\le x+2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind $P(Y<2\\,|\\,X=\\frac{3}{4}).$"] [17592186544823 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be two continuous random variables with the following joint probability density function:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{8}({y}^{2}+x), & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the expression of the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X\\,|\\,Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ for $0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186544859 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=3{x}_{1}(t)+5{x}_{2}(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,x(0)=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the initial value problem above. By applying the Laplace transform to both sides of each equation in our system, we get a transformed system with the solution \n\n$$\n{X}_{1}(s)=L\\{{x}_{1}(t)\\}=\\frac{2}{s-2},\\,{X}_{2}(s)=L\\{{x}_{2}(t)\\}=-\\frac{2}{s-2}+\\frac{1}{s-5}.\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the original initial value problem.\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$x(t)=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{2t}+\\,\\,$</td>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\,\\,{e}^{5t}$</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td height=\"30px\" width=\"5p