nd the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{8}{15}.$"] [17592186546958 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-6x(t)+2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of linear differential equations above?"] [17592186546977 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+y}{3}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{11}{9},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{5}{9},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.5329,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2833,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places."] [17592186546987 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-3x(t)-y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-6x(t)-2y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-5,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[-1,\\text{ }3]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*"] [17592186546989 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y}{{x}^{2}}+\\frac{1}{2}, & \\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{4}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2,\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{7}{12},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2898,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.2764,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places."] [17592186547001 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)-2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=-4x(t)+4y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of linear differential equations above. The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are ${\\lambda }_{1}=0$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=6,$ for which the corresponding eigenvectors are ${v}_{1}=[1,\\text{ }1]^{T}$ and ${v}_{2}=[-1,\\text{ }2]^{T},$ respectively. Which of the following could represent the phase portrait of the system?\n\n*Hint: Here, the dotted line represents the equilibrium solutions.*"] [17592186547013 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-y)}{2}, & \\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2} \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.4332,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.4332,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places."] [17592186547028 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{12}(xy+1), & \\,{y}^{2}\\le x\\le 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nThe joint probability density function $f(x,y)$ for the continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is shown above. Given that \n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]=\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\text{E}[Y]=\\frac{1}{7},\\,\\text{SD}[X]≈0.2619,\\,\\text{SD}[Y]≈0.4238,\n$$\n\n \nfind the correlation coefficient of $X$ and $Y.$ Round your answer to $2$ decimal places."] [17592186547042 "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=x(t)+2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=3x(t)+6y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives all equilibrium points of the system of linear differential equations above?"] [17592186547063 "$$\nf(x,y)=\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})}{\\pi }, & \\,x\\ge 0,\\,y\\ge 0,\\,{